The final content_shell link fails with twelve crash_reporter symbols:

    undefined reference to `crash_reporter::SetCrashReporterClient(...)'
    undefined reference to `crash_reporter::InitializeCrashpad(bool, ...)'
    undefined reference to `crash_reporter::CrashReporterClient::...'  (x10)

This is unfinished business from 0060. That patch stopped content_shell from
depending on the crashpad handler, and content_shell_app already drops
//components/crash/core/app for Haiku a few lines above -- but it left
app/shell_crash_reporter_client.cc in the target's sources. That file
subclasses crash_reporter::CrashReporterClient, so removing the library that
defines the base class leaves its entire vtable undefined, and
shell_main_delegate.cc still calls SetCrashReporterClient/InitializeCrashpad.

Note the exclusion has to go in content_shell_app, which owns those sources,
not in content_shell_lib further down where the other is_haiku `deps -=`
blocks live; GN rejects `sources -=` for an entry the target does not have.

Drop the client source here; U0007 removes the call sites in the vendored
shell_main_delegate.cc. crash_reporter::InitializeCrashKeys() is unaffected --
it comes from //components/crash/core/common:crash_key, which stays.

--- a/chromium/content/shell/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chromium/content/shell/BUILD.gn
@@ -103,6 +103,15 @@
       "//components/crash/core/app:test_support",
     ]
   }
+  if (is_haiku) {
+    # Those deps are what defines crash_reporter::*. Dropping them while still
+    # compiling the client that subclasses CrashReporterClient leaves its whole
+    # vtable undefined at the final link.
+    sources -= [
+      "app/shell_crash_reporter_client.cc",
+      "app/shell_crash_reporter_client.h",
+    ]
+  }
   defines = [
     "CONTENT_SHELL_VERSION=\"$content_shell_version\"",
     "CONTENT_SHELL_MAJOR_VERSION=\"$content_shell_major_version\"",
